From 21c66ef1014554aafbb6b48a0d6b93828ddf67ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:05:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] XHTTP: Show a flow governor client that announces the default
 window all of it

A server with a send window showed its own stack one frame of initial window
whatever the client announced. A client with a governor of its own announces
65535 and counts on every byte of it: it holds back credit under a quantum
while it takes the sender to have a quantum left. At the limit the server
governor kept the other 49151 bytes back, the client governor took them for
window the sender had, and a slow reader whose client cap had shrunk
returned nothing: the download stopped for good.

One frame is now shown only for a client that announces more than the
protocol default. One that announces the default is shown all of it, so the
limit holds nothing back from it: what such a client holds is up to its own
governor.
